{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "193",
   "text": "Do tariffs change the trade balance, and who absorbed the Q4 US demand drop?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "194",
   "text": "Trade scholars assume it is; Setser says not necessarily",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "195",
   "text": "So the tariffs work as a clear tax",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "196",
   "text": "Never stated, but the argument depends on it",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "197",
   "text": "Uncertainty can reduce investment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#P4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "198",
   "text": "~15% average tariff on $500B+ of China imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "199",
   "text": "Govt captures 35bp of the 60bp GDP consumers lose",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "200",
   "text": "Investment slowdowns lead to import slowdowns",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "201",
   "text": "Consumer goods, autos, capital goods all soft",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "202",
   "text": "Far short of the fall in China imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "203",
   "text": "Backdoor fiscal tightening slows consumption",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "204",
   "text": "Especially new business equipment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "205",
   "text": "Weaker investment means fewer imported goods",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "206",
   "text": "Not the argument Trump makes for them",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "207",
   "text": "Imports from other countries stopped making up the gap",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "208",
   "text": "Setser: \"the weakening of U.S. demand was felt globally, rather than in the United States\" US GDP held because services demand stayed strong",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "209",
   "text": "Setser admits he glossed over this too",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "210",
   "text": "Blip or persistent trend? Too early to tell",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "211",
   "text": "Strong dollar, 2018 Fed hikes, shale cutbacks",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_feb_26_20#R1"
  },
